\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Base-model artifact}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{pretraining}
\tag{language-model}

\p{An FTIP \newvocab{base-model artifact} #{M_0} is the pre-post-training
record containing the trained parameter value #{\theta_0}, the architecture
configuration, and the tokenizer model. It also records the context and
numerical conventions required to evaluate #{\pi_{\theta_0}}.}

\p{This is an FTIP working definition, not a standard scalar model
identifier. SentencePiece motivates keeping a self-contained tokenizer model
with the learned system; see \citet{sec. 3.5}{kudo2018sentencepiece}. The
architecture and parameter components follow the decoder-only model in
\citet{sec. 6}{phuong2022formal}. Training data and optimizer provenance may
be attached to #{M_0}, but they are not inputs to one forward evaluation.}
